#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119932 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119506 :question/id #uuid "a67e620f-6380-5754-81db-7e593cdf4336" :question/math-academy-id "e-10998" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ - 4 \\\\ 5\\end{array} \\right]}, \\quad\n\\mathbf{b}=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ - 4\\end{array} \\right]}, \\quad\n\\mathbf{c}=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}, \\quad\n\\mathbf{d}=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}{:}$\n\n$$\nM =\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cccc}2 & 3 & - 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ - 4 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & - 4 & 2 & 5\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M{:}$\n\n$$\nV = | \\det(M) |\n$$\n\nNotice that the $2$nd row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}{2}} & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{-4}} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{5}} & -4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $2$nd row of the $3 \\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-3\\begin{vmatrix}3 & {\\color{lightgray}{-2}} & 1 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 1 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} \\\\ -4 & {\\color{lightgray}{2}} & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3(15+4) \\\\  & =-57.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV = | \\det(M) | = |-57| = 57.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3118d2af-771f-54c9-b18e-5196b87b6dca" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048857 :topic/difficulty 1.0 :topic/id #uuid "c6ca0a0b-f271-529c-9c72-0fa759ec1fda" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100878} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100879}] :topic/math-academy-id 1169 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049339}] :topic/title "The Geometric Interpretation of the 2x2 Determinant"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725788 :question-generator/id #uuid "209cf7ef-fdd7-577b-adc9-a88fa9a87aa8" :question-generator/script "generators/05/05146dfd85ea80bb69e2237e4c2246d9fba2fddb7e928e0ed281a2812ca1ad36/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e95030aa-facc-57bc-a067-bc451ad1374f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117131} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6af53d-7760-5096-8a31-3095f5d9b7de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117132} {:answer/id #uuid "0bc252a8-6719-5235-b5d6-f98d705b4b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117133} {:answer/id #uuid "10728f9e-3b0e-5cc9-8b3f-6335450e726a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117134} {:answer/id #uuid "3a90cfa2-e36f-522c-8364-598f68d52004" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e95030aa-facc-57bc-a067-bc451ad1374f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117131} :answer-field/id #uuid "52b627ee-4bc3-5489-9d76-5cbb1da4554d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117130}] :question/id #uuid "51a08025-ad88-5114-a80b-dc078b5bb9ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-157694" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix $M$ whose columns are $a,b,c,d$. The volume equals $|\\det(M)|$.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=\\begin{vmatrix}2&1&-2&1\\\\0&-1&0&0\\\\-1&1&3&-2\\\\3&2&0&0\\end{vmatrix}\n=-\\begin{vmatrix}2&-2&1\\\\-1&3&-2\\\\3&0&0\\end{vmatrix}\n=-3\\begin{vmatrix}-2&1\\\\3&-2\\end{vmatrix}=-3(4-3)=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is $|-3|=3$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ca47757-6b3a-5772-9af3-09ed4a5523e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272907} {:answer/id #uuid "4502b298-c573-5ffc-ad94-e71a7fe58d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272976} {:answer/id #uuid "478fb4fb-eb8e-587f-9d9e-4e691814f0fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272999} {:answer/id #uuid "df1afce7-376f-54b4-b1dd-527de2c28a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274356} {:answer/id #uuid "e555bfc0-ce1f-5ebf-9618-7b8aa1e9990c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "478fb4fb-eb8e-587f-9d9e-4e691814f0fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272999} :answer-field/id #uuid "90abddc7-2b6e-5be2-982a-3f50ba7107ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274882}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "302209ad-3d64-52f9-9fa9-99104ad6beb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-157695" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=5\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)=-30.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-30|=30.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "478400f5-12d3-537c-9f87-fbc0de611e68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272998} {:answer/id #uuid "79df43db-fad2-5496-a61c-154bea4bfb4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273436} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8588fe-ba26-52d2-96ad-dd3b2374c528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273632} {:answer/id #uuid "a0166d3e-5891-5775-9bb7-edb418a91f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273772} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b4bd2a-0dc8-5886-be0f-d0fa3a157987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79df43db-fad2-5496-a61c-154bea4bfb4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273436} :answer-field/id #uuid "d322600e-3d33-5ca9-9728-eaa166ff5e91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275008}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "210e9083-358f-508e-9376-e356564e0e4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158104" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 7 & 13 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 7 & 13 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2=24.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|24|=24.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27aa8c33-edfb-5fb2-adfb-8de8ec26ee80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272737} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9e26c9-c473-5f4d-8f65-9bd62434b33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273182} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bc95c5-7da6-5228-b9f8-40a00f91ebed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273968} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7acf39-2806-5c1f-bac9-2f76b89d98e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274027} {:answer/id #uuid "dc81e9da-6f65-5e19-8784-3030b7eb61ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc81e9da-6f65-5e19-8784-3030b7eb61ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274324} :answer-field/id #uuid "1470b275-7731-546d-9f3e-40a3009a30fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274671}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "edcd069d-5898-5a9f-9b4f-3515e782b5c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-158106" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=3\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot (-2)=-72.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-72|=72.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8d63a0-e6e8-5621-b14e-0a6afb7468b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272792} {:answer/id #uuid "4e356ba3-0766-580b-b544-969b6db926d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273046} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9af943-2e3a-56aa-a3d4-69f1c9aa6ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273306} {:answer/id #uuid "7b178126-366e-5772-8fae-0734a917447f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273443} {:answer/id #uuid "e3683848-ab39-5f23-91ed-e22f1d4d80fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a9af943-2e3a-56aa-a3d4-69f1c9aa6ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273306} :answer-field/id #uuid "16f94c49-7116-5254-8071-00edbc36756c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274676}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32e6e8c1-9b26-5825-ac5f-18dfd683a674" :question/math-academy-id "q-158108" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}=7\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 5=-105.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-105|=105.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c55fd61-b7c5-584d-8bde-77e2feec81f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272636} {:answer/id #uuid "85bb8804-af94-50ef-9fa7-689080c4022c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273537} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7b9016-9a9f-57ae-89d0-4f976fd13493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274167} {:answer/id #uuid "e82989cc-6d2