448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14dc93bc-a38e-5377-a83e-cdfd8429aad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272575} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfab9dd-4d38-5d0a-8ae4-4bb8f2dfb58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272627} {:answer/id #uuid "51509c36-6629-523a-8205-b2bb3effda20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273079} {:answer/id #uuid "7aeddc74-6832-5dcd-b316-c663fd53aeae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273441} {:answer/id #uuid "7e044c6a-8d91-53c4-961f-fd4db697aee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bfab9dd-4d38-5d0a-8ae4-4bb8f2dfb58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272627} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc8de92-2ed5-584b-9065-852c4f8079e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274653}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4e39b2b-6ddb-522a-a369-dfb16a50311d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158110" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 12 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 12 & 5\\end{bmatrix}=6\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 5=-180.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-180|=180.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275449 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ade1b1c2-bb18-5ec5-a08e-f2fe191dfc0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273887} {:answer/id #uuid "d02cdc25-7525-505a-846a-c4d1135329bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274202} {:answer/id #uuid "d235c9d6-d0dd-5309-9d9d-e70481f4d759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "154" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274224} {:answer/id #uuid "f06e744b-0c4e-56b4-9ccf-073c04c36996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274515} {:answer/id #uuid "f7eafda1-95e4-50d3-9e5d-c6169be19dbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "134" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d02cdc25-7525-505a-846a-c4d1135329bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274202} :answer-field/id #uuid "f95e766c-71b6-5648-a6e3-04cdaca450da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275075}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3a8456a-5f67-54bf-8d0a-07a8bbe82bf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-158114" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $2$nd row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}{3}} & -2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{-2}} & 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{4}} & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-2\\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}{-2}} & 1 & 5 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{1}} & 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-6\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-6(4-25) \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|126|=126.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e51492-c3b7-54b6-8660-3327203595bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272699} {:answer/id #uuid "28eeb732-2c18-5922-b6a9-bbd2d7eec5d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272751} {:answer/id #uuid "3084793d-d7d4-5080-9297-c5dbc7fc686c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272817} {:answer/id #uuid "b981ba03-1c73-5fee-958e-9f516f79590f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273996} {:answer/id #uuid "ed17d628-c951-506b-b286-13e3eb6a5ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23e51492-c3b7-54b6-8660-3327203595bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272699} :answer-field/id #uuid "56164ca7-3d80-5b0c-bf3e-27409397895a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274782}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c594e512-d19a-53c5-8f50-4caaf295111c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158368" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $3$rd column of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 1 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{1}} & {\\color{lightgray}{4}} & 3 & {\\color{lightgray}{6}} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =3\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-120|=120.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275469 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049a84c1-52fe-5a96-80d0-bdfba1ece812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272428} {:answer/id #uuid "2e002483-bff0-5696-8b17-34e6d65302e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272797} {:answer/id #uuid "650c50e4-830c-5672-a10f-2d86d1f80ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273251} {:answer/id #uuid "686c0b94-d2c7-570f-a49e-0b44f7a5e887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273289} {:answer/id #uuid "f965d840-d861-5dd1-be3a-b2a400272e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f965d840-d861-5dd1-be3a-b2a400272e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274574} :answer-field/id #uuid "6428d2da-cec3-5130-8fdf-f3195ddd3a25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274807}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d7bd54b-d293-5ee2-b790-9af4e0cb0ced" :question/math-academy-id "q-158369" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=3\\cdot 5\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 3=-45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-45|=45.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb8b630-1858-5675-a8ea-afd745123540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272641} {:answer/id #uuid "25136c9e-920f-566e-a408-ea4a7af1ef37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272712} {:answer/id #uuid "28f41079-6423-5124-b7dd-2b748bc5ac50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272753} {:answer/id #uuid "37c41e9d-c90b-5532-80b8-70fb57bf191a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "176" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272875} {:answer/id #uuid "39e96dc4-16ab-55e3-b742-85d0597e033b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39e96dc4-16ab-55e3-b742-85d0597e033b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272890} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a3f55ee-40e6-566b-9375-89a8f6437390" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274708}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94fb05dd-7b6c-5fef-becd-0abc3ccf0dc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-158371" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $1$st row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 2 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} \\\\ -2 & {\\color{lightgray}{7}} & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & {\\color{lightgray}{5}} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & {\\color{lightgray}{5}} & 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $2$nd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 10 & {\\color{lightgray}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & {\\color{lightgray}{2}}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =8\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =8(-14+30) \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|128|=128.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ca3fc2b-bad0-5b4b-bc00-408085561cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369847} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c7791b-9b12-5dd6-9d19-547ef87dd6a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369848} {:answer/id #uuid "c232025a-ca14-5a4a-9e9f-a8ff81b74a6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369849} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6c71c2-2201-52f2-abf4-3b33cdc6feea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369850} {:answer/id #uuid "1571cd95-16d4-5e7a-a516-2378f040ff5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ca3fc2b-bad0-5b4b-bc00-408085561cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369847} :answer-field/id #uuid "10725161-b676-53dc-8bff-5c967c1e8dfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fc304b0-a53d-5a62-b8cd-1ca341a43179" :question/math-academy-id "q-158367" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $4$th row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & {\\color{lightgray}{5}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & {\\color{lightgray}{7}} & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & {\\color{lightgray}{-2}} & 2 & 1 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & -1 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & {\\color{lightgray}{0}}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-12|=12.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da1aec45-a768-5bc0-8b78-ec818aed675a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369854} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5fcf24-0e46-5b4b-9678-6276ff3944ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369855} {:answer/id #uuid "326d3d9a-2161-5ea5-a630-9abd2df1cb38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369856} {:answer/id #uuid "c014177e-0ec9-57d0-9ab5-61d474743308" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369857} {:answer/id #uuid "12bbbdba-f568-5df7-bc40-4fdfb1daeda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c014177e-0ec9-57d0-9ab5-61d474743308" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369857} :answer-field/id #uuid "190a5c0e-6b81-53d6-b669-800a2e45a632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369853}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47b0b8bf-3751-5718-9c72-c6b036aa4e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-158370" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c},$ and  $\\mathbf{d}:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $2$nd column of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & -3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 7 & 2 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{0}} & 2 & {\\color{lightgray}{1}} & {\\color{lightgray}{1}}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd column of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} \\\\ 7 & 5 & {\\color{lightgray}{0}} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}{10}} & {\\color{lightgray}{7}} & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(15+21) \\\\  & =144.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|144|=144.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3194d732-4a27-57e4-90b5-376278b1fad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429806} {:answer/id #uuid "3c025708-e1f6-590a-bdc9-0995f51cbaec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429807} {:answer/id #uuid "a745ff62-0494-5386-bded-3bb0f59f39cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429810} {:answer/id #uuid "f1560774-e64f-5713-95be-58cfbace4e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429813} {:answer/id #uuid "fb522c79-1eec-53f4-a1ce-a41acd3ad978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1560774-e64f-5713-95be-58cfbace4e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429813} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b729052-de1a-56fa-9f79-cc8f868046e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429815}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d62e579-1b65-5746-996a-3e6e877f180c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158107" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,c=\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 & 13 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 & 13 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=(-7)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 1=-70.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-70|=70.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186647767 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a06fffe-06c9-55bc-a50e-e7fa49d2872e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647342} {:answer/id #uuid "775f4aa1-c326-51ae-a861-e3b35c95cf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647372} {:answer/id #uuid "9d79cb0c-9e63-5c24-9f66-b25fdf691500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647456} {:answer/id #uuid "a0707554-3eb0-5147-8431-6821c022b04d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647460} {:answer/id #uuid "edbcc83a-eb99-5505-bb92-f96068ad6f7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0707554-3eb0-5147-8431-6821c022b04d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647460} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3337707-d4d9-5f91-8406-a7c390b905c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647740}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "301d0715-4815-5daf-8034-fe65846710a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-158111" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,c=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 7 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 7 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=(-9)\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot 2=54.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|54|=54.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32a2c5c2-65ec-585a-9345-d61f6f73f5b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703745} {:answer/id #uuid "79c6cc1b-7142-5f63-a62d-2440398ef1a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703752} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4ce473-99e5-52dd-856a-ca29eaac8804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703753} {:answer/id #uuid "7f21afa1-4070-51d9-8097-6bfdeae34f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703754} {:answer/id #uuid "a54bf5d6-4644-5100-ab38-c1e9bb5d47fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a4ce473-99e5-52dd-856a-ca29eaac8804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703753} :answer-field/id #uuid "290ba7f4-af53-5cd2-a00a-bb99aaa9b3d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703743}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "395a5b70-ac13-5278-8751-fd5d50d0bc64" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nThe matrix is not triangular. Its first row has two nonzero entries, so expansion along that row has two contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=1\\cdot D_1-2\\cdot D_2,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD_1=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\qquad D_2=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand each minor along its first column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_1&=1(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}=1\\bigl(-1+2\\bigr)=1,\\\\D_2&=2(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}=-2\\bigl(-1-4\\bigr)=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions before taking the absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=1-2(10)=-19,\\qquad V=|-19|=19.\n$$\n\nTaking the absolute value of each contribution separately would give $1+20=21$, which is not the absolute value of their signed sum."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a11b86d-da87-571e-bda6-56bc21226885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703744} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce740a4-3f52-5848-be09-199b3bdbce26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703755} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b24014-dd55-5147-959b-46eda9f4c2f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703756} {:answer/id #uuid "afa3fbe6-d88f-59bd-ade0-080f6da16c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703759} {:answer/id #uuid "fec3c119-3709-5de8-82a9-8dfef5e95d91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4b24014-dd55-5147-959b-46eda9f4c2f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703756} :answer-field/id #uuid "b278e873-b98c-501b-8180-2f69d83ed102" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703760}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50253898-a808-5160-9504-e6d09cb4773b" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nThe second row has only one nonzero entry. Expand along that row, retaining the cofactor sign:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=2(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe third row of this minor also has only one nonzero entry. Expand along that row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(M)&=-2\\cdot 3(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=-6\\bigl((-1)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2\\bigr)\\\\&=-6(-7)=42.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|42|=42.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdc24d1-eac9-5cc4-8ea9-152bcc16ea68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703742} {:answer/id #uuid "5a5168d7-a4b3-5328-b0b1-53f7b59c31e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703749} {:answer/id #uuid "69e1454b-43ca-5525-b829-c2998a9bc1b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703750} {:answer/id #uuid "6f947f10-28e5-5d6d-8f90-d739b490cc1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703751} {:answer/id #uuid "cab7a91e-b3e0-5a17-b344-4fed25fa3050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bdc24d1-eac9-5cc4-8ea9-152bcc16ea68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703742} :answer-field/id #uuid "5525553c-bad2-5290-99a9-33ede2072b40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703748}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad064368-6ced-56a0-a3c2-6b304c0cf688" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nThe matrix is upper triangular, so its determinant is the product of its diagonal entries.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-2)\\cdot 3\\cdot 1\\cdot 2=-12.\n$$\n\nA volume cannot be negative, so\n\n$$\nV=|-12|=12.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4398d6bc-928d-5f62-a985-9b2c125cec24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704224} {:answer/id #uuid "65a83798-c150-5915-aa63-5c2634cd0573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704227} {:answer/id #uuid "78744a08-5dba-5cb4-ad4a-e4614372254f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704229} {:answer/id #uuid "ac1ef642-cb73-501a-ac06-2d1a7082b198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704237} {:answer/id #uuid "c528a85b-adfc-5ed5-a8e9-92425b500451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65a83798-c150-5915-aa63-5c2634cd0573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704227} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba2d121-5a52-57cc-b274-bd496df29d72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704230}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "074e6459-9745-5e96-8c1a-f4f1590214b1" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $3$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=1(-1)^{2+3}D_{1}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis matrix is triangular, so multiply its diagonal entries.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=(-2)\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-4)=-24.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-1)\\cdot (-24)=24.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|24|=24.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f0b6db-9b2d-5324-ac9f-3aa1fe394c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704215} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc1dd64-a799-5d62-b324-ffa2a26a2896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704221} {:answer/id #uuid "778865f2-2fef-5374-ad1d-e77242e7fc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704228} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5b27f7-2e6a-59b5-9ee8-8d5aa7eb7ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704240} {:answer/id #uuid "c81bff2c-3bc0-5cc9-b812-63fc66ef8503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07f0b6db-9b2d-5324-ac9f-3aa1fe394c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704215} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa59a708-7cfb-5339-9c9c-e863df9dc95e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704248}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f29876a-cadf-5a2c-a2a6-6871f0037edc" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $3$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-1)(-1)^{4+3}D_{1}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis matrix is triangular, so multiply its diagonal entries.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=2\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-2)=16.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=1\\cdot 16=16.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18a9f21a-f605-5182-813d-b11ac681088b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704218} {:answer/id #uuid "25b9d554-d9a2-52e9-9f31-eacc28f43ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704222} {:answer/id #uuid "360674a2-e064-5e11-b6d8-58d765f2c187" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704223} {:answer/id #uuid "532f6c38-8d3f-5584-a27c-73ceecbd5cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704225} {:answer/id #uuid "815f3e8b-4309-5a2e-aacb-f774f8aa81b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18a9f21a-f605-5182-813d-b11ac681088b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704218} :answer-field/id #uuid "61b28845-74d8-5d42-b935-a67934f3e898" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704226}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8772a75a-be80-5415-8086-84f3ea4af0d8" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along row $3$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-3)(-1)^{3+2}D_{1}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along row $3$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=(-2)(-1)^{3+2}D_{2}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{2}&=(-2)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1\\\\&=(-6)-1=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{1}=2\\cdot (-7)=-14.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=3\\cdot (-14)=-42.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|-42|=42.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a088fbd-1625-5109-b4c0-d895155e4a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704219} {:answer/id #uuid "1c073555-788b-57aa-814d-e3f3bb4a1656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704220} {:answer/id #uuid "a91ce31c-5feb-53e3-bbf3-4bbff8c9175f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704236} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9adb06-342f-5237-9814-0a3978023376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704239} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c57f19-b66a-53d2-82dc-b4f100862b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a088fbd-1625-5109-b4c0-d895155e4a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704219} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd6c800-5260-5a9d-9c6a-0d8faf6d67a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704241}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8edf5ac0-ceb8-5d68-b7b3-ee5e04414f11" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $1$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=1(-1)^{3+1}D_{1}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis matrix is triangular, so multiply its diagonal entries.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=3\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 4=-36.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=1\\cdot (-36)=-36.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|-36|=36.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1794ae4d-f103-5226-a922-bc99ea7ce66d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704217} {:answer/id #uuid "818ffea5-794f-57e2-a435-9004a41c9403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704233} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fd1034-cc1b-5d32-b093-55a8f06d77d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704238} {:answer/id #uuid "e063a629-734a-570d-8412-90cd91e73cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704245} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b19110-0f1a-5b68-b490-7c687fb884e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8fd1034-cc1b-5d32-b093-55a8f06d77d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704238} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c945ada-9e70-5675-a4e5-da9265b30ebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704216}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf25b63d-57c2-5edb-a678-1c0b35ea1a89" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along row $3$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=3(-1)^{3+4}D_{1}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $1$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=(-3)(-1)^{2+1}D_{2}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{2}&=4\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1\\\\&=8-1=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{1}=3\\cdot 7=21.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-3)\\cdot 21=-63.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|-63|=63.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b40157f-c160-53e2-9d02-046394d4fec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704261} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7d4aeb-1dc8-5dc9-800b-d381ec2fe92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704263} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f63996-c829-5936-8958-1f5181d21e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704267} {:answer/id #uuid "bb15cf05-4b2b-5183-b733-dae88ba98f4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704268} {:answer/id #uuid "fcffb5d5-27ce-56f8-b9ee-7ae5d7995f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb15cf05-4b2b-5183-b733-dae88ba98f4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704268} :answer-field/id #uuid "f526f7be-01b4-5787-a45b-e7519ad76c54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704275}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "14474f3f-fe50-5bb7-8cd7-4828d0fc3003" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along row $4$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-1)(-1)^{4+1}D_{1}+3(-1)^{4+3}D_{3}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $2$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=(-4)(-1)^{1+2}D_{2}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{2}&=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot (-1)\\\\&=4-2=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{3}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $1$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{3}=(-3)(-1)^{2+1}D_{4}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{4}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{4}&=(-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1)\\\\&=(-4)-(-1)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{3}=3\\cdot (-3)=-9.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{1}=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=1\\cdot 8+(-3)\\cdot (-9)=35.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|35|=35.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704265 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ee69ed8-9df6-57a9-96f3-91f9c25f8bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704255} {:answer/id #uuid "21e04442-ee31-5011-8b67-9a4d9133a190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704256} {:answer/id #uuid "5ada9fc5-da68-5378-9dc7-6db6b5da3c0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704260} {:answer/id #uuid "6fcaff27-222b-5245-984d-36c4169481a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704262} {:answer/id #uuid "fadb4b5a-150f-5c8e-aa97-f59369399769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21e04442-ee31-5011-8b67-9a4d9133a190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704256} :answer-field/id #uuid "844aaad4-518c-5e0b-8198-448464b93d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704264}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87421bbb-1864-5d1b-8d4e-c61630b4ef86" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along row $4$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-1)(-1)^{4+2}D_{1}+4(-1)^{4+4}D_{3}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $3$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=2(-1)^{1+3}D_{2}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{2}&=4\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-3)\\\\&=4-(-9)=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{3}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $2$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{3}=3(-1)^{3+2}D_{4}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{4}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{4}&=3\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 4\\\\&=9-4=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{3}=(-3)\\cdot 5=-15.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{1}=2\\cdot 13=26.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-1)\\cdot 26+4\\cdot (-15)=-86.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|-86|=86.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0638a4f5-b667-5182-a6f4-acb888daf41e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704250} {:answer/id #uuid "102b8f65-f694-53a8-859b-a7ea412ce863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704252} {:answer/id #uuid "8e06bd71-d275-5ebd-924d-d0ae62c5da94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704266} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e4fbeb-e8f1-55fe-86ea-60cce8d36294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704270} {:answer/id #uuid "d0401953-c1d9-5d12-a97c-2b61eaa03203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e06bd71-d275-5ebd-924d-d0ae62c5da94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704266} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd0e1080-8df8-53b0-b296-5dd773af6fb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704269}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9d09386-de39-5fdc-9879-c52d570701e5" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along row $2$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=(-4)(-1)^{2+1}D_{1}+1(-1)^{2+2}D_{3}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $1$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=1(-1)^{2+1}D_{2}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{2}&=4\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 1\\\\&=4-1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{3}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $1$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{3}=3(-1)^{1+1}D_{4}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{4}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{4}&=(-2)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 1\\\\&=(-2)-(-2)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{3}=3\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{1}=(-1)\\cdot 3=-3.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=4\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 0=-12.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|-12|=12.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b5a93b-1155-5146-ad1d-a1fdc7b48334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704251} {:answer/id #uuid "11e4c8ba-c7fe-5967-8673-f50ae3995dc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704253} {:answer/id #uuid "46046cce-0a82-5360-8c82-7a741236e851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704258} {:answer/id #uuid "4efbc344-aff5-51f6-95d1-12239fe83868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "280" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704259} {:answer/id #uuid "d725df19-2ad7-5b47-91f7-660415165860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d725df19-2ad7-5b47-91f7-660415165860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "168" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704272} :answer-field/id #uuid "3100fda9-b7de-5f45-84e6-800b6091831d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704257}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f013bdf4-d9f1-56eb-85be-ba0e2e35ddff" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{c}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{d}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Construct the matrix whose columns are the four vectors:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe volume is the absolute value of its determinant:\n\n$$\nV=|\\det(M)|.\n$$\n\nExpand along row $1$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=2(-1)^{1+1}D_{1}+(-4)(-1)^{1+4}D_{3}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{1}=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $3$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{1}=(-1)(-1)^{1+3}D_{2}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{2}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{2}&=3\\cdot 4-(-4)\\cdot 4\\\\&=12-(-16)=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{3}=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpand along column $1$, retaining the cofactor signs.\n\n$$\nD_{3}=(-2)(-1)^{2+1}D_{4}.\n$$\n\nEvaluate the minor\n\n$$\nD_{4}=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the difference of the cross products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{4}&=4\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 4\\\\&=16-(-12)=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{3}=2\\cdot 28=56.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\nD_{1}=(-1)\\cdot 28=-28.\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\det(M)=2\\cdot (-28)+4\\cdot 56=168.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nV=|168|=168.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Volume of an N-Dimensional Parallelepiped"}]}
